# Orange fill vs text-link hover

Orange fill (`--primary-color`) plus white text is **selection only**.
Do not use that fill as the default link hover.

## Selection

```css
::selection,
*::selection {
    background: var(--primary-color) !important;
    color: #fff !important;
}
```

Same for `::-moz-selection`. `!important` is required.

## Text links

Orange text. Hover underlines. No background.

```css
a.text-link,
main a:not(.dl-btn):not(.dn-btn) {
    color: var(--primary-color);
}

a.text-link:hover,
main a:not(.dl-btn):not(.dn-btn):hover {
    color: var(--primary-color) !important;
    background: none !important;
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 0.18em;
}
```

Do not set `color: #fff` on a text-link hover. That was the old fill hover.

## Not text links

Buttons, nav icons, cards, and the donate-banner CTA keep their own hover.
Those may use orange fill. Text on that fill stays white.

Never set `a:hover { background: transparent }` globally. Download and
donate actions are `<a class="dl-btn">`. That rule wipes the orange
fill and leaves white text on the card.

Keep the global rules in `static/css/custom.css` and theme `_misc.scss`.
